ook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>SHINOZAKI HIROSHI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>TAHARA KAZUO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>TAKAKURA YUHACHI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>ISHII, MAKOTO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KAWABATA, YUKIO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>NOTOHARA, YASUO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SHINOZAKI, HIROSHI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TAHARA, KAZUO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TAKAKURA, YUHACHI</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A position detection circuit and a motor control device capable of providing a rotor position detection signal accurately over the entire PWM control area and providing the same signal even during a PAM control; specifically, a brushless motor control device which controls current supply to a stator winding by detecting the position of a magnetic pole of the stator based on a terminal voltage of a stator winding in each phase, wherein a comparison result information signal obtained by comparing a detection voltage corresponding to the above terminal voltage with a reference voltage is directly input to a control circuit to accurately detect the rotor position of the motor immediately after current supply switching without providing a rotor position detection inhibiting period and to control the motor accurately.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention porte sur un circuit de détection de position et sur un dispositif de commande de moteur fournissant un signal précis de position du rotor sur la totalité de la zone de commande MID et fournissant ce même signal même pour la commande de moteurs PAM. L'invention porte spécifiquement sur un dispositif de commande de moteur régulant l'alimentation en courant des enroulements statoriques en détectant la position d'un pôle magnétique du stator en fonction de la tension aux bornes de l'enroulement pour chaque phase. On introduit ensuite dans le circuit de commande un signal résultant de la comparaison entre la tension aux bornes détectée et une tension de référence, ce qui permet une détection précise de la position du rotor immédiatement après la coupure de l'alimentation en courant sans période d'interruption de la détection de la position du rotor, ainsi qu'une commande précise du moteur.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>